cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use System One Bench or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "System One Bench: an independent benchmark for decision models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alhashimi
    given-names: Ali
repository-code: "https://github.com/alilibx/system-one-bench"
url: "https://systemonebench.dev/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  System One Bench scores decision models, which read a state and answer typed questions (yes/no, one of several
  options, or an ordered score) with probabilities in one call. Every model gets byte-identical requests on frozen
  data: 3,250 text cases across 16 labelled datasets in English, French and Arabic, and 1,200 image cases across
  6 datasets. Models are scored on accuracy, calibration, latency and cost.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - decision models
  - calibration
  - multilingual
  - Arabic
  - vision
